\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come in, O come! The door stands
\par open now;
\par I knew Thy voice; Lord Jesus, itwas Thou.
\par The sun has set long since; the storms begin:
\par 'Tis time for Thee, my Saviour;
\par O come in!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I seek no more to alter things, 
\par or mend,
\par Before the coming of so great a Friend:
\par All were at best unseemly; and 
\par 'twere ill,
\par Beyond all else, to keep Thee waiting still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Then, as Thou art, all holiness and bliss,
\par Come in, and see my chamber as it is;
\par I bid Thee welcome boldly, 
\par in the name
\par Of Thy great glory and my want
\par and shame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come, not to find, but make, this troubled heart
\par A dwelling worthy of Thee as Thou art;
\par To chase the gloom, the terror,
\par and the sin,
\par Come, all Thyself, yea come, 
\par Lord Jesus, in!
\par                 Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

